      [
        'Use calibrated claims and discipline-appropriate register.',
        'Make reference chains and agency clear.',
        'Distinguish language precision from unnecessary complexity.'
      ],
      'Academic English makes claims and relationships assessable. In an invented report, The trial recorded higher attendance accurately names an observed result. The trial suggests a possible access benefit adds a qualified interpretation. The trial proves universal learning improvement overstates what attendance measures. Discipline conventions differ: active voice and first person can be appropriate when they clarify methods. A reference chain such as attendance counts → these counts → this measure keeps the topic identifiable. Nominalization can name an abstract process, but excessive abstraction can hide agency: The implementation of recording occurred is less clear than The team recorded visits. Precision includes clear scope, defined terms and justified hedging.',
